      "message": "[info] Line 319: The `ice_msg` check reliably distinguishes a genuine PeerConnectionRequest from a TrustRequest unpacked via MSGPACK_DEFINE_MAP (TrustRequest has no `ice_msg` key, so it stays empty), which is a good discriminator. However, this branch also fires for connection *answers* (`isAnswer \u003d\u003d true`), since only `connType` and `ice_msg` are inspected. Receiving a push for an answer would now spin up the daemon and trigger a full sync (loadAll). Consider guarding with `!peerCR.isAnswer` if answers are not expected to require daemon startup here, or add a comment explaining why answers are intentionally handled the same way.",
